From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:28:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] feat(users): let admins disable and enable accounts

An account that must stop signing in (someone who left, a suspected
compromise) could only be deleted, or locked by hand in the database.

PATCH /api/users/:id now also takes `disabled`. Disabling sets
users.disabled_at (a nullable column: an expand step), ends every
session and raises the securityVersion in one transaction, so the
person is signed out everywhere at once. While it is set, sign-in
answers exactly as for a wrong password (SessionsService.create refuses
it, whichever flow signs in), refresh and the access-token guard refuse
it too (also when the column was set by hand), and password recovery
sends nothing and refuses a link sent before. Nobody disables their own
account; the last admin who may sign in cannot be disabled or demoted.

The account's page shows its status and disables it after a
confirmation, or enables it again; the list of users has a status
column.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
