+### Disabled accounts
+
+An admin disables an account from its page (`PATCH /api/users/:id` with `disabled: true`), after
+confirming; nobody disables their own account, and the last admin who may sign in cannot be
+disabled. In one transaction under the account's lock, `users.disabled_at` is set, every session
+ends and `security_version` rises, so the person is signed out everywhere at once. While it is
+set:
+
+- sign-in answers exactly as for a wrong password (`SessionsService.create`, which every way of
+  signing in goes through, refuses it), so the page tells nobody the account exists or is
+  disabled;
+- refresh and `JwtAuthGuard` refuse it too, even when the column was set by hand without the rest;
+- password recovery sends nothing, as for an unknown address, and a link sent before is refused:
+  the account keeps its password.
+
+Enabling it (`disabled: false`) lets the person sign in again with that password; nothing else
+comes back.
+
